            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## Orbit 0.1.2

### New

- **Chromium 158.** Orbit moves from Chromium 156 to 158, with its security fixes.
- **A Help menu.** Send Feedback writes a mail to us with Orbit's log attached, and Known Issues opens the list of what the beta doesn't do yet.
- **Move to Applications.** Opened from the disk image, Orbit offers to move itself, and Check for Updates says why when it can't check.
- **About Orbit** shows the third-party notices and Chromium's credits, and where the source code is.

### Safer

- A page that goes full screen is named on a card for a few seconds, so a site cannot pretend to be another.
- A long address keeps its end, so the real site is always the part you see.
- Downloaded files lose the characters in their names that can disguise what kind of file they are.
- After a crash, your tabs come back asleep, so a page that crashed Orbit cannot do it again at every launch.
- The crash report you choose to send says where Orbit crashed and what kind of error it was, never the error's message.

### Fixed

- Closing a tab never closes its window, and closing the last window asks first while downloads are running.
- Signing in to a streaming site no longer bounces back and forth.
- A tab whose site may send notifications no longer goes to sleep.
- A pinned site changing its icon or title no longer holds up the window.
- A link that opens Orbit is no longer lost when your windows are restored.
- The usage counts question on first run has two equal answers.
]]></description>
